      "body": "# [AMD] Add FlyDSL DSA MQA-logits backend\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe DSA sparse indexer is a major GLM-5.2 long-prefill cost on MI355X. Merged\n[ROCm/aiter#4538](https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/4538) provides a FlyDSL FP8\nMQA-logits kernel that is faster than the currently used Triton implementation\nat the production 32k EXTEND shape.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `--dsa-mqa-logits-backend` with `auto`, `triton`, and `flydsl` choices.\n- Preserve Triton as the default.\n- Allow FlyDSL only on ROCm gfx950.\n- Route both non-chunked and memory-bounded chunked HIP MQA-logits calls\n  through the selected backend.\n- Preserve `clean_logits=False` and the existing downstream masking/top-k\n  contract.\n- Add CPU tests for backend resolution and unsupported-platform rejection.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAll four registered backend-dispatch tests pass. The merged AITER #4538 matrix\npassed 56/56 eager and 56/56 graph-replay cases on gfx950, covering supported\nhead shapes, FP8 payloads and scales, and causal, context-parallel, misaligned,\nempty, and past-end windows.\n\nExact-head 60k-input/600-output eager serving completed with the FlyDSL backend.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nHardware: AMD MI355X, TP4, `amd/GLM-5.2-MXFP4`, FP8 KV cache, AITER DSA\nprefill, TileLang DSA decode, and 32,768-token prefill chunks. Candidate and\ncontrol differ only in `--dsa-mqa-logits-backend flydsl` versus `triton`.\n\nMatched pure-32k EXTEND stage traces:\n\n| Variant | MQA logits | Complete DSA indexer | Prefill wall |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Baseline Triton | 94.7981 ms | 178.5417 ms | 1682.2568 ms |\n| FlyDSL | 92.1294 ms | 175.5948 ms | 1681.6625 ms |\n\nFlyDSL reduced MQA-logits time by 2.82% and complete DSA-indexer time by 1.65%.\nPrefill GPU wall was neutral at -0.04%.\n\nMatched 60k/c4 serving:\n\n| Metric | Triton | FlyDSL | Change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Output throughput | 119.5089 tok/s | 120.0747 tok/s | +0.47% |\n| Mean TPOT | 26.0681 ms | 26.1603 ms | +0.35% |\n| Mean TTFT | 3767.9743 ms | 3640.1554 ms | -3.39% |\n\nThe serving run used 60,000 input tokens, 600 output tokens, concurrency 4,\nseed 15, and 32 prompts after an unrecorded warmup.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nLaunch the candidate on MI355X:\n\n```bash\nSGLANG_USE_AITER=1 python3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model amd/GLM-5.2-MXFP4 \\\n  --tp 4 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --attention-backend dsa \\\n  --dsa-prefill-backend aiter \\\n  --dsa-decode-backend tilelang \\\n  --dsa-mqa-logits-backend flydsl \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\\n  --page-size 64 \\\n  --disable-shared-experts-fusion \\\n  --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 256 \\\n  --disable-radix-cache \\\n  --chunked-prefill-size 32768 \\\n  --max-prefill-tokens 32768\n```\n\nFor the matched control, change only `--dsa-mqa-logits-backend` from `flydsl`\nto `triton`. Run a 60k-input/8-output warmup at concurrency 4 and seed 0,\nfollowed by 60,000 input tokens, 600 output tokens, concurrency 4, seed 15, and\n32 prompts.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format and code-style checks pass.\n- [x] Add unit coverage for backend resolution.\n- [x] Run the registered test on the exact rebased head.\n- [x] Run exact-head MI355X eager and graph validation.\n- [x] No user-facing documentation change is required.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36826029257](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36826029257)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36826028988](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36826028988)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36826029276](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36826029276)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
